# ========================
# Dot-directories (IDE, cache, config)
# ========================
.*/
*.md
!README.md
!docs/**/*.md
!backend/app/engine/models/families/*/vendor/*.md

# ========================
# Backend data directories
# ========================
backend/datasets/
backend/outputs/
/outputs/
backend/venv/
# Throwaway venv clones used to test dependency upgrades without mutating the
# working environment (e.g. the transformers 5.x upgrade). Multi-GB — an
# unignored clone turns any `git add -A` into a catastrophic commit.
backend/venv-*/
backend/models/
backend/.*
backend/settings.json
backend/server.log
backend/server.prev.log
backend/restart.log
backend/tests/tests.log
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# ========================
# Workspace-level directories
# ========================
# `_docs/` is the INTERNAL documentation tree — audits enumerating weaknesses in
# this codebase (some unfixed) and internal plans. It was called `docs/` until
# 2026-09-01, when the public documentation took that name to match the GitHub
# convention (LANE-62). Ignored as a whole DIRECTORY, which is the strongest
# form available: git does not descend into it, so nothing inside can be
# resurfaced by a later re-include, deliberately or by accident.
_docs/
/adapters/
/scripts/
graphify-out/

# ========================
# Python
# ========================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
*.egg
dist/
build/
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.bin
*.pth

# ========================
# Node / Angular
# ========================
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.angular/

# ========================
# OS files
# ========================
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ========================
# Environment & secrets
# ========================
*.env
.env.*

# MRLN-Harness (imported by _harness/tools/import_harness.py)
_harness/
.agent/workdir/
.agent/output/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# ========================
# Public surface allowlist (MUST STAY LAST — last match wins)
# ========================
# `origin` is public, so "tracked" means "published". Three blanket rules above
# hold the private surface back: `.*/` (line 4), `*.md` (line 5) and `/docs/*`.
# They stay. The public surface is re-included here, explicitly and by name.
#
# RULE: re-include a DOCUMENT BY NAME, never a DIRECTORY — with ONE deliberate
# exception, `!docs/**/*.md` on line 7, which carries the public documentation.
# The rule's evidence still holds: a directory re-include publishes whatever is
# added to that directory later, by anyone, with no review step and no diff that
# reads as a disclosure. It was measured — a `!docs/` re-include once published
# 169 files, including audits enumerating unfixed weaknesses and internal plans.
# What changed on 2026-09-01 (LANE-62) is WHERE that material lives: it is now
# under `_docs/`, ignored as a whole directory above, so `docs/` is public by
# CONSTRUCTION rather than public by exception. The residual risk is real and
# named: anything dropped into `docs/` is published without a name-level gate.
# Keep internal material in `_docs/`; if that ever stops being reliable, revert
# to per-name re-includes here.
# `LICENSE` needs no entry here: it has no extension, so no rule matches it.
!.github/
!.github/**
!SECURITY.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!CHANGELOG.md
# API_CONVENTIONS.md, LOGGING.md and TESTING.md are INTERNAL (`_docs/`) as of
# 2026-09-02, on the user's word: "we will not publish the harness". They were
# re-included here briefly by the release-hardening pass; nothing under docs/
# was ever pushed, so nothing public changed.
# `documentation/` no longer exists: ARCHITECTURE.md moved to `docs/` and the
# user chose a clean rename over a redirect stub (LANE-62, 2026-09-01).
